from pathlib import Path
import re,html,difflib,markdown,json,hashlib
O=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;R=O.parents[3]
def render(s):return markdown.markdown(re.sub(r'<!--\s*@[^>]*-->','',s),extensions=['extra','sane_lists'])
def image(n,caption):return '<figure><a href="'+n+'.png"><img loading="lazy" src="'+n+'.png" alt="'+html.escape(caption,quote=True)+'"></a><figcaption>'+caption+'</figcaption></figure>'
before=(O/'Color_Context_Placed.before.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8');after=(R/'commons/maps/Color_Context_Placed/final.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
assert after==(O/'Color_Context_Placed.after.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
a=before.split('\n\n');b=after.split('\n\n');pairs=[]
for tag,i,j,k,l in difflib.SequenceMatcher(None,a,b,autojunk=False).get_opcodes():
 if tag=='equal':continue
 pairs.append('<div class="pair"><div><h3>Before</h3>'+(render('\n\n'.join(a[i:j])) or '<p>New shared illustration.</p>')+'</div><div><h3>Now</h3>'+render('\n\n'.join(b[k:l]))+'</div></div>')
css=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',(O.parent/'2026-09-23-array-molnar-volume/index.html').read_text(encoding='utf-8'),re.S)[1]
page='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Colour — another way to gather</title><style>'+css+'</style></head><body><main>'
page+='''<div class="eyebrow">Ada Research · Colour · 23 September 2026</div><h1>Another way to gather.</h1><p class="intro">The parts touch in one order.<br>Colour lets you gather them in another.</p><p class="status">Applied to <strong>Color_Context_Placed/final.md</strong>. Two paragraphs and one sentence sharpen the existing encounter. The working columns now supply two shared book illustrations.</p><nav><a href="#encounter">Four rules</a><a href="#scale">Walk around it</a><a href="#comparison">What changed</a><a href="#reading">Read the hall</a><a href="#evidence">Evidence</a><a href="/compose/sources?map=Color_Context_Placed&amp;doc=final">Read and comment</a></nav>'''
page+='<section id="encounter"><h2>The form stays. Its company changes.</h2>'+image('four-colour-rules','The same five forms under the four placed colour assignments. These are native views inside the museum, with the same camera offset relative to each column. Existing lighting varies across the hall.')+'<p>The red block above the sphere can belong with the red blocks below it. Nothing needs to move for the eye to find that relation. The code gives each piece a colour according to a chosen rule: one value, its kind, its height, or the colour below.</p></section>'
page+='<section id="scale"><h2>The movement is yours</h2>'+image('around-the-rainbow','The fixed 6.2-metre rainbow column from two selected camera positions, each 1.65 metres above its base. The same six-colour order repeats five times around the shaft.')+'<details><summary>From the entrance to whole configurations</summary>'+image('hall-entrance','The current museum entrance, looking towards the later combinations.')+image('whole-configurations','Two and three gallery configurations become the final 7.2- and 7.4-metre columns. This is a selected overview camera, not a recorded player journey.')+'</details><p>The larger stacks remain part of the chapter. They give the earlier primitives, transformations and arrays room to become compositions, with colour both calculated and associated.</p></section>'
page+='<section id="comparison"><h2>A small return to a mature hall</h2><p>The opening now returns directly from the disco floor. The first comparison asks the reader to follow red across an intervening blue sphere. The rainbow passage describes stripes entering and leaving view, rather than suggesting a new set of colours. All three code excerpts, both artifact sections, the art and design references, the scientific and associative discussion, and the handoff to illumination remain.</p><details open><summary>Original and current passages</summary>'+''.join(pairs)+'</details><p><a href="Color_Context_Placed.diff">Exact manuscript diff</a> · <a href="source-changes.diff">Companion and record changes</a></p></section>'
page+='<section id="reading"><article class="reading">'+render(after)+'</article></section>'
page+='''<section id="evidence" class="evidence"><h2>What was checked</h2><p>24 focused checks pass in the isolated production museum: all 23 column studies load, the opening four have the same local forms and transforms, and their assigned-colour counts are one, two, five and two. The tall studies retain their intended heights; the rainbow remains fixed between views. Native captures and final compositions were inspected.</p><p>The figures crop, resize and label actual Godot renders. The first camera setup looked through the entrance doors; it was moved inside and the final-stacks view widened. No production geometry, material assignment, placement, control or sequence was changed.</p><p>This pass does not repeat the <a href="/book-review/doc/book/iterations/2026-09-23-colour-gathering/SUMMARY.md">earlier route work</a>. These photographs and state checks do not establish headset comfort, physical reach, walking or a reader’s experience. The rendered colours are subject to the hall’s illumination and the display.</p><p><a href="report.json">Focused runtime record</a> · <a href="source_manifest.json">Capture inputs</a> · <a href="verification.json">Preservation and publication checks</a> · <a href="SUMMARY.md">Findings and decisions</a></p></section><footer>Next: Color_Flashlight. Keep the receiving surface and move the light.</footer></main></body></html>'''
(O/'index.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
paths=['commons/maps/Color_Context_Placed/intent.md','commons/maps/Color_Context_Placed/tutorial.md','commons/maps/Color_Context_Placed/field_notes.md','commons/data/museum_core_encounters.json']
diffs=[]
for p in paths:
 diffs.extend(difflib.unified_diff((O/'before'/p).read_text(encoding='utf-8').splitlines(True),(R/p).read_text(encoding='utf-8').splitlines(True),fromfile='before/'+p,tofile=p))
(O/'source-changes.diff').write_text(''.join(diffs),encoding='utf-8')
(O/'publication-sources.json').write_text(json.dumps({p:hashlib.sha256((R/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in ['commons/maps/Color_Context_Placed/final.md']+paths},indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
print('Built current reading and comparison page.')
